From 5314248e319eca368e68c2a019ca75ed6a25ddbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafig <rafig12332@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:01:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(desktop): make ADR-0191's XAML audits executable, and
 fix the six defects they find
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ADR-0191 recorded that "where a class of defect can be caught statically, it
now is: a StaticResource audit over the views, and a scan for DataContext
overrides that shadow a sibling binding, both run clean over every view in the
repository." Neither existed as a script, a test or a gate. It had been one
person reading files once, and the decision expired the day it was written.

XamlContractTests is that audit, executable: six tests over every .xaml in the
shell project. File scanning, not WPF — no PresentationCore, no dispatcher, no
window — so it runs in the headless suite on any platform in about a tenth of a
second. XML comments are blanked before scanning, so a file that explains a
defect is not read as having one. A sixth test asserts the audit actually read
the views, because the other five pass trivially over an empty list.

Run against the released markup it failed with six findings.

The tab-strip idiom the handoff carried forward was in four workspaces, not
two. Tag is typed object, so <Trigger Property="Tag" Value="True"> compares a
boxed bool against the string "True" and never matches: CustomersView,
FinanceView, PurchasingView and WarehouseView, twenty-seven buttons in total,
rendered with nothing selected in every theme.

Two instances of the shadowing class had never been recorded at all.
StocktakesView and TransfersView bind a detail card's Visibility to
IsDetailOpen on the element that also sets DataContext="{Binding Detail}".
IsDetailOpen belongs to WarehouseCountsViewModel and
WarehouseTransfersViewModel, not to the detail view models, so the binding
resolved against the child, failed silently, and left the card permanently
visible over a register with nothing selected — the Finance defect exactly,
inside a Functional Alpha already claimed.

All six are fixed: the four strips use the DataTrigger form Employees
introduced, and the two cards are rooted through their UserControl.

ADR-0208 records the audit and the structural rule it enforces — a binding
beside a DataContext override states its own source — chosen over "bind to a
property the child has" because only the structural form is enforceable.
Fifteen of the repository's seventeen DataContext overrides already complied;
the two that did not were the two defects.

Verified on Linux: solution build and desktop/src/Qrafig.Desktop build 0
warnings / 0 errors with EnableWindowsTargeting; Qrafig.UnitTests 59/59;
Qrafig.Desktop.Tests 1068 total, 1059 passing, the 9 failures being the
documented DPAPI platform baseline and the identical set that failed before
this change; has-pending-model-changes reports no changes; no vulnerable
packages across all 14 projects. Not run: Qrafig.IntegrationTests and
Qrafig.Desktop.EndToEndTests (no Docker daemon) and the live QRAFIG.exe smoke
(no Windows host). Neither covers this change, and the ledger says so.

